 Services Sexual Assault & Relationship Violence Support Resources Mental Health Services Be an Active Bystander Frontline Responders Fire Prevention Police Services Public Safety Regional Campus Security Quick Links Annual Security Reports Emergency Planning Guides Flash ALERTS Important Phone Numbers Threatline FlashLine Login Calendars Phone Directory Maps & Directions Search Apply Visit Give Now Employment Kent About Employment There are so many things that make us undeniably Kent State. From our vastly different culture full of visionary ideas to our highly ambitious students, faculty and staff, we’re a special place with a welcoming atmosphere. And we’re always looking for those who may be a fit for us. Full- and Part-time Employment Are always available. And we offer ample resources to assist faculty and staff in professional and personal development. More information about employee development can be found on our Division of People, Culture and Belonging page. Interested in working with us? We’d love to hear from you. See current openings Student Employment We’re proud to employ more than 5,000 students in more than 8,000 positions across our eight campuses. On­-campus work allows students to enjoy flexible hours and supportive supervisors and to develop skills, explore career options and gain references. It’s all in the name of creating their brightest future possible. For more information, view the Checklist for Students for obtaining employment on campus or contact us at the Career Exploration and Development . Search and apply for ON-CAMPUS EMPLOYMENT About Why Kent State? University Information Information For Ways to Engage Explore About Academics Admissions Alumni Athletics Campus Safety Jobs & Employment Life at KSU Locations News Our Research Need Help? Request Admissions Information For the Media Website Feedback Policies and Compliance Annual Security Reports Campus Concerns Reporting Privacy Statement Senate Bill 1 Compliance Web Accessibility Co